{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"29a33fdb60fb062e","type":"text","text":"==Recreation==","x":-121,"y":-26,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"80779c254a3d8d88","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> ==Once between hunts==, the entire group may optionally choose one of the following ==recreation== activities and take the associate keycard, answering the attached questions and exploring the answers. This provides a little downtime to the exorcists and allows them to develop their characters and relationships outside of the stresses and confines of a hunt. Your group may enjoy it for the pacing change or just the opportunity to show a different side of their characters.","x":129,"y":-520,"width":411,"height":360},
		{"id":"fc266d99a093e9e8","type":"text","text":"Personnel who had already passed their simulacrum operation must be already familiarized with our prepared installations for training, special recovery and social interaction with other operative teams.\n\nTeams are allowed to request transference to one of our installations in Europe for such benefits with a duration between a few days up to a week, in correspondence with how much \"free time\" is available to the team before the next operation.","x":-360,"y":-500,"width":411,"height":280},
		{"id":"207a43c38368ac97","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> There are a couple caveats: \n> \n> • The group must agree on the ==same activity==, and it costs nothing. \n> • Exorcists may choose to ==split== from the group and choose a different activity. If they do, they must pay 1 scrip, even if someone has already bought access to their chosen activity. \n> • If an activity specifies morning or evening access only, ==one time period== must be chosen. This mainly changes the setting of the scenes and how exorcists might handle their time during recreation.","x":84,"y":-1020,"width":501,"height":360},
		{"id":"19e1d9f26da45e80","x":-338,"y":-971,"width":367,"height":311,"type":"text","text":"*The Administration wants to remind you:*\n\n*Higher than allowed logistical workload increase will be authorized with a minimal transaction of one kind of file or access code back to logistic reintegration.*\n\n*Please clarify time of arrival for the sake of allowing better organization in both logistical and operational departments.*\n\n*We are truly grateful for having you back willingly, operative.*"},
		{"id":"8aea4473e4d7ea97","x":98,"y":-1540,"width":473,"height":350,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Exorcists must be well behaved during recreation. Every area has security cameras and keycard access doors that limit who can come and go. Letting in personnel not approved for keycard access, tampering with surveillance equipment, damaging facilities, leaving facilities untidy, or taking items out of facility areas is punishable by ==sanction== and bans activities completely for offending exorcists for the next period between hunts. Exorcists subject to sanction more than once or who break sanction severely are docked scrip for additional violations (usually 1 or 2) or disciplined."},
		{"id":"9bfc1e326b0d60a5","x":-353,"y":-1505,"width":398,"height":280,"type":"text","text":"*The Administration wants to remind you:*\n\n*Although recreational activities are allowed and even sometimes even expected for social growth with those in the same state that you, be aware that any structural, material or organic damage in a minor or mayor scale will be properly sanctioned for the team or individuals involved in the incident.*\n\n*We are truly grateful of your presence and care in avoiding any unnecessary trouble, operative.* "},
		{"id":"2c9593908b0663b7","x":-60,"y":-1940,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Options for this are present in pages 41 to 45!"}
	],
